WEBVTT

00:05.060 --> 00:08.639
Hello, everyone. We're
the three-piece girl band...

00:08.640 --> 00:09.230
First Astronomical Velocity!

00:09.230 --> 00:10.900
First Astronomical Velocity x15

00:09.231 --> 00:10.810
First Astronomical Velocity!

00:11.690 --> 00:13.290
I'm band leader and bassist Suzu Fujimi.

00:12.610 --> 00:14.280
Suzu Fujimi (Bass)

00:12.610 --> 00:14.210
I'm band leader and bassist Suzu Fujimi.

00:14.610 --> 00:17.819
I handle guitar and vocal duties...

00:15.610 --> 00:17.280
Super Sonico (Vocals/Guitar)

00:17.820 --> 00:19.200
I'm Super Sonico!

00:19.530 --> 00:23.870
And on taiko... I mean, on
DRUMS, I'm Fuuri Watanuki.

00:23.250 --> 00:24.920
Fuuri Watanuki (Drums)

00:24.160 --> 00:27.909
First Astronomical Velocity will be
holding its regularly scheduled show

00:27.910 --> 00:31.130
this coming May 24th, at
SuperNova in Akihabara.

00:31.420 --> 00:36.129
Doors open at 6:00, show starts at 6:30.
Entry and a free drink for just 2,000 yen!

00:36.130 --> 00:42.090
If you're even a little curious,
come watch and have a great time with us!

00:42.260 --> 00:46.009
We'll fill you up with, like, a
cotton candy kind of power!

00:46.010 --> 00:48.139
Huh. I'm not sure what that means.

00:48.140 --> 00:52.399
If you don't come, I don't know how
I'll afford to eat next month...

00:52.400 --> 00:53.979
That was strangely serious.

00:53.980 --> 00:58.319
Well, in any case, please don't forget
our regularly scheduled show.

00:58.320 --> 01:00.610
We hope to see you all there!

01:04.240 --> 01:09.079
I was so nervous! Do you
think we got it right, Suzu?

01:09.080 --> 01:11.420
Uh, Nico, the camera's still rolling.

01:12.790 --> 01:16.420
U-um! Thank you all very much!

01:19.800 --> 01:21.299
Ippai hibiki MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

01:21.300 --> 01:22.799
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

01:22.800 --> 01:24.299
Ippai todoke FEELING
Let tons of feelings reach you

01:24.300 --> 01:25.799
Super Soni let's go!

01:25.800 --> 01:27.259
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

01:27.260 --> 01:28.786
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

01:28.810 --> 01:30.389
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

01:30.390 --> 01:32.640
Super Soni LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

01:44.620 --> 01:49.080
Saikin omoitsukimashita
Lately, I've come to realize

01:50.700 --> 01:55.040
Kimochi tsutaeru tte taihen
That getting feelings across is tough

01:56.790 --> 02:01.589
Umaku dekitari dekinattari
Whether it goes well or not

02:01.590 --> 02:05.339
Muzukashii kara oku no te de
Is tough, so my trump card

02:05.340 --> 02:07.930
Mouretsu taiatari desu
Is going for it at full force

02:09.680 --> 02:11.980
Dakedo hitomishiri (hitomishiri)
But I'm shy (shy)

02:12.600 --> 02:15.400
Gomakashite senobi (senobi)
I act like it's nothing and aim high (high)

02:15.770 --> 02:17.309
Ashi ga gakuburu de
With legs trembling

02:17.310 --> 02:20.570
Hirakinaotte arinomama GO!
I get serious and just go for it!

02:20.940 --> 02:23.569
Zenkai, soukai, daitenkai Recuperation,
exhilaration, a big revolution

02:23.570 --> 02:26.620
Nandemo chokushin STRAIGHT
No matter what, keep heading straight

02:26.950 --> 02:29.619
Sekai, mankai, mugendai
The world, in full bloom, infinity

02:29.620 --> 02:33.159
Kyou mo genki ni koko ni imasu (HEY!) I'm
here again today, living to the fullest (Hey!)

02:33.160 --> 02:34.686
Ippai hibike MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

02:34.710 --> 02:36.119
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

02:36.120 --> 02:37.766
Ippai todoke FEELING?
Let tons of feelings reach you

02:37.790 --> 02:39.039
Super Soni let's go!

02:39.040 --> 02:40.709
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

02:40.710 --> 02:42.049
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

02:42.050 --> 02:43.856
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

02:43.880 --> 02:46.050
SUPER SONI LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

03:04.320 --> 03:05.359
Nice, nice!

03:05.360 --> 03:07.699
I'd say we have the new
song down, wouldn't you?

03:07.700 --> 03:13.699
Uh... But was the refrain good? I don't
think I came in hard enough at the hook.

03:13.700 --> 03:16.750
Can I change out the
effects unit and try it again?

03:17.120 --> 03:18.000
Okay.

03:18.001 --> 03:19.629
Roger that, my friend.

03:19.630 --> 03:20.710
Sorry.

03:21.920 --> 03:24.460
Nico, you're all fired up, huh?

03:24.760 --> 03:29.639
Like my grandma always says,
"Do what you can with all you've got."

03:29.640 --> 03:33.100
"What you can with all you've got," huh?
That's you, all right.

03:33.470 --> 03:35.790
You're giving your modeling
job "all you've got" too, huh?

03:34.690 --> 03:35.610
MAJOR PRIZES!!

03:42.270 --> 03:44.899
Wh-wh-why do you have that, Suzu?!

03:44.900 --> 03:47.819
I was SO embarrassed when I bought it.

03:47.820 --> 03:50.200
Then you shouldn't have bought it!

03:53.200 --> 03:55.040
It's already time, huh?

03:55.160 --> 04:01.210
Yup. It's been two hours already.
I could tell by how hungry I am.

04:02.710 --> 04:05.089
That's convenient, but
sort of troublesome, too.

04:05.090 --> 04:07.169
Wanna go get something to eat?

04:07.170 --> 04:08.629
We can have a meeting, too.

04:08.630 --> 04:09.870
Meat sauce?!

04:09.871 --> 04:14.520
First Astronomical Velocity

04:10.220 --> 04:12.010
MEETING, I said!

04:16.100 --> 04:19.310
So, here's the set list I'd
like to use for our next show.

04:19.810 --> 04:23.939
We should save the new song for last, and
maybe do "Passion Rocket" for the encore.

04:23.940 --> 04:26.189
We can open with "Skylab Hurricane."

04:26.190 --> 04:30.529
I think it's a great list!
What do you think, Fuuri?

04:30.530 --> 04:32.409
I'm with Suzu!

04:32.410 --> 04:34.160
Then it's settled.

04:34.530 --> 04:37.500
I'll handle the tickets
and the posters, too.

04:37.700 --> 04:39.709
Thanks for always doing that.

04:39.710 --> 04:43.590
No worries. I'm the only one who can
properly use a computer, anyway.

04:44.170 --> 04:47.800
Speaking of, Fuuri, did you finish that
drawing for our new merchandise?

04:48.550 --> 04:50.880
Drawn to order, I'd say.

04:51.430 --> 04:52.430
Ta-daa!

04:53.220 --> 04:57.020
It's so cute! Your drawings
are always great, Fuuri.

04:57.770 --> 05:01.730
It turned out good this time.
The lines of his tummy are especially...

05:05.690 --> 05:10.699
How cruel! The only way to ease this
sadness... is to ORDER ANOTHER SERVING!

05:10.700 --> 05:12.320
Redraw it, right now!

05:13.490 --> 05:16.660
By the way, Nico, I'd like
to ask you about something.

05:17.160 --> 05:18.409
What is it?

05:18.410 --> 05:21.499
I'd like to update your
stage outfit for next time.

05:21.500 --> 05:25.339
Huh? Only me? What about you and Fuuri?

05:25.340 --> 05:28.170
The outfit really only fits YOU.

05:28.300 --> 05:31.129
An illustrator friend of mine designed it,

05:31.130 --> 05:35.429
and I had a cosplay maker near
my work do it for me on the cheap.

05:35.430 --> 05:37.470
Here it is! Your costume!

05:37.970 --> 05:41.480
Wow, it's fantastic! So cute!

05:42.890 --> 05:48.480
And that's not all. This outfit has
its own gimmick to draw in more fans.

05:48.820 --> 05:50.069
A gimmick?

05:50.070 --> 05:53.110
Yup. It's made of a special cloth.

05:56.240 --> 06:00.830
As it absorbs more of your
sweat, it will slowly melt away.

06:01.200 --> 06:03.290
Then, at the climax...

06:05.830 --> 06:08.500
the audience's
"voltage" hits a climax, too!

06:10.010 --> 06:14.089
Forget it! I'm not doing
that! You can just forget it!

06:14.090 --> 06:15.589
Come on!

06:15.590 --> 06:16.850
Forget it!

06:18.180 --> 06:19.349
Now, Suzu...

06:19.350 --> 06:24.899
I understand you made that costume to give
the people at our shows a good time,

06:24.900 --> 06:29.070
but it's NICO who'll be wearing it, so you
have to consider her feelings, too.

06:29.730 --> 06:31.359
But I already made it!

06:31.360 --> 06:33.029
Even so, this won't do.

06:33.030 --> 06:34.529
It's a matter of priorities.

06:34.530 --> 06:40.410
We put on shows so people can listen to our
music, not just look at what we're wearing.

06:40.990 --> 06:42.700
Fine, I get it!

06:42.950 --> 06:46.790
I'll have them make it with normal
cloth in time for the show.

06:48.670 --> 06:50.640
- ZEPPELIN
- PUB

06:48.670 --> 06:50.089
TODAY'S SPECIALS

06:50.090 --> 06:53.800
Suzu always comes up
with the funniest ideas.

06:54.170 --> 07:00.179
It's nothing to laugh about, Grandma!
I could never wear that, not even for Suzu.

07:00.180 --> 07:05.349
Huh? You should've accepted the challenge!
I'd sure like to see that naughty outfit!

07:05.350 --> 07:07.690
Hey! That's sexual harassment!

07:05.980 --> 07:07.690
HABANERO

07:07.980 --> 07:11.689
Still, Leyla was quite the
challenger back in the day.

07:11.690 --> 07:13.439
Grandma was?

07:13.440 --> 07:17.160
It was a long time ago, mind you.
When we were young,

07:17.450 --> 07:20.780
the shopping district merchants took
a trip out to the beach.

07:21.080 --> 07:23.620
You should've seen Leyla back then!

07:24.580 --> 07:28.000
"It's the very latest thing!" she said.

07:28.710 --> 07:31.549
Wow... That really happened?

07:31.550 --> 07:36.720
Back then, I was up for doing anything
if I thought it sounded fun.

07:37.010 --> 07:39.139
You're the same way, Sonico.

07:39.140 --> 07:41.680
Isn't that why you and the
others formed your band?

07:43.270 --> 07:45.180
Yeah, I guess so. You're right!

07:45.430 --> 07:46.809
Do your best.

07:46.810 --> 07:47.810
Sure!

07:51.570 --> 07:53.439
That's spicy! So, so spicy!

07:53.440 --> 07:55.739
You shouldn't tease a young girl.

07:55.740 --> 07:57.700
Water! Get him some water!

08:04.500 --> 08:07.290
SONG TITLE:
FIRST
ASTRONOMICAL
VELOCITY

08:16.890 --> 08:19.970
<i>DOLPHIN CRIES ARE
AN EXCHANGE OF
BURST-PULSE SOUNDS</i>

08:25.850 --> 08:27.890
FIRST ASTRONOMICAL VELOCITY
REGULARLY SCHEDULED SHOW

08:33.450 --> 08:35.490
FIRST ASTRONOMICAL VELOCITY
REGULARLY SCHEDULED SHOW

09:04.180 --> 09:06.509
The food there was great, huh?

09:06.510 --> 09:08.429
Yeah, I'd like to go again.

09:08.430 --> 09:09.600
Speaking of...

09:10.100 --> 09:11.389
Look over there, Yumi.

09:11.390 --> 09:12.390
Hm?

09:13.190 --> 09:14.190
Ah!

09:16.320 --> 09:17.320
Ah!

09:18.070 --> 09:20.529
Sonico's acting weird...

09:20.530 --> 09:21.910
What's she doing?

09:22.280 --> 09:25.119
Oh! Actually, THAT'S soon, isn't it?

09:25.120 --> 09:26.120
Yeah.

09:26.620 --> 09:27.620
Sonico?

09:29.500 --> 09:30.710
What are you doing?

09:31.250 --> 09:35.629
It's not so much what I'm doing...
I haven't really done anything at all.

09:35.630 --> 09:38.169
But I have to do it! But...

09:38.170 --> 09:39.880
Can we have two?

09:40.130 --> 09:42.430
That's it, right? Your live set.

09:43.010 --> 09:45.850
H-how did you know that?

09:46.720 --> 09:49.390
Because you always act weird before a show.

09:49.770 --> 09:51.730
She's easy to read, huh?

09:52.140 --> 09:52.600
BAND
CLUB

09:52.601 --> 09:55.149
You're sure we can have all these for free?

09:55.150 --> 10:02.319
Yes! I owe you all for letting me practice here
so often, even though I'm not a band member.

10:02.320 --> 10:05.029
We look forward to it every time...

10:05.030 --> 10:08.280
both your set and what
you wear when you play, Nico!

10:10.160 --> 10:12.619
I wouldn't get my hopes up about that...

10:12.620 --> 10:14.919
Well, have you decided?

10:14.920 --> 10:17.380
We'd still like for you to join our club.

10:19.840 --> 10:27.259
I'm very grateful for the offer, but First
Astronomical Velocity is the only band for me, so...

10:27.260 --> 10:28.260
I see.

10:28.640 --> 10:30.890
So, will you practice today after this?

10:31.180 --> 10:35.809
Um, no. I promised to meet
everyone at the studio later.

10:35.810 --> 10:40.820
That's too bad. We always have more
members show up when you're here.

10:47.370 --> 10:48.989
Yes, hello?

10:48.990 --> 10:50.869
Sonico? It's Kitamura.

10:50.870 --> 10:53.620
Oh, Mr. Manager. Yes, what is it?

10:54.080 --> 10:56.369
Are you done with your classes for today?

10:56.370 --> 10:57.000
Yes.

10:57.001 --> 10:59.589
I'm sorry to spring this
on you so suddenly,

10:59.590 --> 11:02.550
but we've found ourselves short a model.

11:03.130 --> 11:06.129
Could you show up for a shoot at 5 p.m.?

11:06.130 --> 11:08.510
Today? Um, today is...

11:08.760 --> 11:10.470
Um, well...

11:10.930 --> 11:13.890
Your tone tells me you
have a prior engagement.

11:14.640 --> 11:17.559
It was unreasonable of me.
Please don't worry about it. Well, then...

11:17.560 --> 11:18.560
Manager?

11:18.560 --> 11:19.230
Hm?

11:19.231 --> 11:22.280
Are there any other models you can get?

11:22.860 --> 11:24.400
I'm about to make some calls.

11:26.240 --> 11:27.699
If you'll excuse me...

11:27.700 --> 11:28.700
Um, wait!

11:28.780 --> 11:30.030
I'll do it!

11:31.530 --> 11:32.450
You're sure?

11:32.451 --> 11:37.370
Yes, it'll be fine. I have to be
at the office by 5 p.m., right?

11:37.750 --> 11:39.420
Okay, understood.

11:53.010 --> 11:54.180
Suzu!

11:54.770 --> 11:55.730
Telephone.

11:55.730 --> 11:56.390
Huh?

11:56.391 --> 11:57.640
Sonico's on the phone.

11:57.890 --> 11:59.190
Nico is?

11:59.810 --> 12:01.899
Suzu here. What's up, Nico?

12:01.900 --> 12:03.070
Um, well...

12:03.440 --> 12:04.570
I'm sorry!

12:04.900 --> 12:11.369
I suddenly got called into work. Do you think
it's all right if I miss practice today?

12:11.370 --> 12:12.409
HUH?!

12:12.410 --> 12:15.410
I really am sorry! The truth is...

12:16.450 --> 12:22.040
Oh, I see. Well, I guess you don't have
much choice, huh? Understood. Roger!

12:22.630 --> 12:25.509
Oh, and I'll tell Fuuri for you.

12:25.510 --> 12:26.420
Okay.

12:26.421 --> 12:27.669
Good luck at work!

12:27.670 --> 12:29.970
Thanks. I'm sorry.

12:32.180 --> 12:36.520
I'm sorry, Suzu. I'm sorry, Fuuri.

12:37.520 --> 12:39.480
Oh, no!! I have to hurry!

12:48.320 --> 12:51.530
I think Sonico looks a little down today.

12:52.240 --> 12:54.989
Ah! But I think we're
getting some good photos.

12:54.990 --> 12:58.119
Still, it's a feature on
maid outfits aimed at girls,

12:58.120 --> 13:00.249
so I was hoping for more of a happy feeling,
something different from the everyday norm.

13:00.250 --> 13:02.169
It seems she forced herself to cancel her other appointment. so I was hoping
for more of a happy feeling, something different from the everyday norm.

13:02.170 --> 13:03.379
It seems she forced herself to
cancel her other appointment.

13:03.380 --> 13:06.750
Her concern over that is
showing in her expression!

13:07.800 --> 13:09.010
Sonico!

13:09.970 --> 13:11.049
Y-yes?

13:11.050 --> 13:12.890
Why don't we take a break?

13:18.060 --> 13:19.640
So, Sonico?

13:20.480 --> 13:22.730
Is there anything you've been
looking forward to lately?

13:23.520 --> 13:25.150
Looking forward to...?

13:25.770 --> 13:27.480
Yeah. A live set.

13:27.780 --> 13:29.439
Huh. Whose?

13:29.440 --> 13:32.529
Ah! Actually, I'll be performing in it.

13:32.530 --> 13:35.700
Sonico, you play music? What genre?

13:36.030 --> 13:37.159
Rock!

13:37.160 --> 13:38.490
Wow...

13:38.910 --> 13:43.210
I've always loved rock. My grandma
taught me how to play guitar,

13:43.670 --> 13:46.790
and I'd wanted to form
a band for a long time...

13:47.380 --> 13:49.339
But I'm kind of shy.

13:49.340 --> 13:51.259
Then how did you form your band?

13:51.260 --> 13:57.510
Well, Suzu... That's the leader of
our band. She invited me to join.

13:58.720 --> 14:00.849
Why'd I ask Nico to join the band?

14:00.850 --> 14:05.940
Yeah. You didn't really know her, right?
So, why did you ask her to join?

14:06.650 --> 14:08.190
Hm, well...

14:08.900 --> 14:11.030
I'd gone to see a concert.

14:11.900 --> 14:15.700
There was this high-school girl who
was really pacing at the entrance.

14:16.160 --> 14:20.540
She looked alone, and it seemed like she was
trying to decide whether to go in or not.

14:20.910 --> 14:23.750
I just couldn't take my eyes off her.

14:27.750 --> 14:29.210
Those boobs are HUGE!

14:30.090 --> 14:36.720
No, I'm kidding. Just by looking at her, I
could tell that this girl really loved music.

14:36.930 --> 14:38.600
So, I started talking to her.

14:39.180 --> 14:40.600
Do you like rock?

14:44.060 --> 14:45.650
U-um...

14:46.980 --> 14:49.270
Yes. I love it.

14:50.820 --> 14:53.030
Listening to it? Or playing it?

14:55.530 --> 14:57.410
U-um, both.

14:57.820 --> 14:58.780
What do you play?

14:58.781 --> 14:59.910
The guitar.

15:00.240 --> 15:01.739
What music do you play?

15:01.740 --> 15:08.129
Um, w-well... All kinds. Of music. So...

15:08.130 --> 15:09.130
Huh?

15:11.960 --> 15:14.419
Ah! What is it? What's wrong?

15:14.420 --> 15:19.389
E-excuse me. I'm sorry! I... I...!

15:19.390 --> 15:21.470
Nico suddenly started to cry.

15:22.180 --> 15:25.520
She looked so helpless
all alone at that club.

15:25.940 --> 15:29.270
And she seemed really
happy that I talked to her.

15:29.610 --> 15:33.610
So we watched the show together, and on
the way back, I just kind of blurted out:

15:34.190 --> 15:37.240
"Hey, wanna join a band?"

15:37.910 --> 15:41.529
Kinda strange, isn't it? I had
no idea she was that good.

15:41.530 --> 15:44.869
Wow, you rock! So then, what about Fuuri?

15:44.870 --> 15:46.210
Oh, Fuuri?

15:46.460 --> 15:51.129
I was walking around Akiba, and a really scary
guy was trying to force her to come with him.

15:51.130 --> 15:52.300
Without thinking...

15:52.630 --> 15:56.300
ATTACK!

16:00.090 --> 16:01.890
I sort of kicked him.

16:02.390 --> 16:07.019
She and I became friends, and when we played
a drum game, I saw she was really good.

16:07.020 --> 16:09.100
So I made her a member.

16:09.690 --> 16:11.479
Wow, you rock.

16:11.480 --> 16:12.520
Right?

16:14.980 --> 16:17.950
I see! So, that's how you formed your band.

16:18.240 --> 16:22.370
Now that you've told me, I understand.
Those members are good people.

16:25.120 --> 16:27.910
Yes! They're wonderful!

16:28.080 --> 16:30.290
They're my dearest friends!

16:42.140 --> 16:45.220
Sorry I'm late, Suzu! And Fuuri...

16:55.610 --> 16:56.530
Nico?

16:56.531 --> 16:57.859
Oh, Suzu? Where are...

16:57.860 --> 16:59.109
In a taxi!

16:59.110 --> 17:00.110
Huh?

17:00.530 --> 17:02.199
It looks like the trains stopped.

17:02.200 --> 17:03.909
Fuuri's totally stuck!

17:03.910 --> 17:04.910
Huh?!

17:05.370 --> 17:10.000
The taxis and buses are full, so she
can't get one. I'm on my way to her now.

17:10.160 --> 17:13.080
Once I get her, we'll race back over there.

17:13.250 --> 17:17.379
Until we get there, rap or sing a cappella!
Whatever it takes. Just buy us time for the show!

17:17.380 --> 17:22.800
Oh, I put your new outfit in the waiting
room locker. There's the station! I gotta go!

17:24.260 --> 17:25.260
Suzu?!

17:31.770 --> 17:33.479
Ten minutes to show time.

17:33.480 --> 17:36.150
Ah! Okay, got it!

17:38.190 --> 17:39.490
I have to do it.

17:39.940 --> 17:42.360
Everyone's waiting in there.

17:50.500 --> 17:51.880
FIRST ASTRONOMICAL VELOCITY

17:52.120 --> 17:53.210
Sonico!

17:55.460 --> 17:58.550
Everyone, thank you all for coming.

17:58.920 --> 18:05.469
I'm Super Sonico, guitarist and vocalist for
three-piece girl band First Astronomical Velocity.

18:05.470 --> 18:08.970
I hope you have a wonderful time tonight!

18:11.180 --> 18:14.230
Ah! Um, actually, we...

18:14.770 --> 18:22.770
Uh, since some of you may not know, I would
like to explain the origin of our band's name.

18:23.570 --> 18:28.779
We call ourselves First Astronomical Velocity
because that's the speed a rocket reaches

18:28.780 --> 18:31.516
when it breaks free of Earth's gravity
to deliver a satellite into space.

18:31.540 --> 18:34.209
It was our leader, Suzu,
who came up with it.

18:34.210 --> 18:39.669
She said we would race at first astronomical
velocity toward the stars... we'd BE stars!

18:39.670 --> 18:44.969
But, apparently, you can't really penetrate the
atmosphere at first astronomical velocity...

18:44.970 --> 18:49.470
What's more, if we were actual
stars, we'd probably just burn up.

18:52.520 --> 18:53.850
Well, don't go burning up!

18:54.600 --> 18:56.809
Hey, Sonico! Where are the others?

18:56.810 --> 18:58.650
Ah! Well, about that...

18:58.900 --> 19:06.069
Th-the truth is, Suzu and Fuuri, the other
band members, are running late. I'm very sorry!

19:06.070 --> 19:07.109
It's okay!

19:07.110 --> 19:08.070
Hang in there!

19:08.071 --> 19:09.240
We'll wait for 'em!

19:09.530 --> 19:14.869
Um, but they should be arriving shortly.
Please, do not be alarmed.

19:14.870 --> 19:19.710
I will be on my own until they arrive,
but I'll do the best I can.

19:20.000 --> 19:22.710
I hope you all will
give this song a listen.

19:23.340 --> 19:27.509
This is our very first song,

19:27.510 --> 19:31.349
which the three of us all worked on shortly
after forming First Astronomical Velocity.

19:31.350 --> 19:32.720
It's called...

19:34.600 --> 19:36.310
Hey, wanna join a band?

19:36.810 --> 19:37.770
Huh?

19:37.771 --> 19:42.690
I play bass and we have a drummer.
But we don't have a guitarist.

19:43.360 --> 19:45.240
So, wanna play with us?

19:45.820 --> 19:47.030
Suzu...

19:48.320 --> 19:51.699
Allow me to introduce you.
This is our drummer, Fuuri Watanuki.

19:51.700 --> 19:53.330
How do you do?

19:53.540 --> 19:58.870
M-my name is Super
Sonico. I-it's a pleasure!

20:03.090 --> 20:05.420
You're hungry, aren't you?

20:05.720 --> 20:10.889
They say that if you share a meat bun
with someone you'll become friends, Sonico!

20:10.890 --> 20:12.100
Fuuri...

20:12.390 --> 20:14.639
Huh? Me, write the lyrics?

20:14.640 --> 20:19.100
Yup. Our rock will be complete
once we add your lyrics.

20:20.270 --> 20:23.520
Nico, I bet your lyrics are yummy!

20:24.480 --> 20:26.900
Understood. I'll give it a shot!

20:34.950 --> 20:36.159
Sonico...

20:36.160 --> 20:37.250
Sonico.

20:45.760 --> 20:48.510
It's no good. I...

20:49.430 --> 20:50.470
I...!

20:57.890 --> 20:59.020
Fuuri!

21:02.440 --> 21:03.480
Suzu!

21:13.700 --> 21:14.780
Everyone!

21:15.030 --> 21:20.250
I'm sorry things ran late.
Without further delay... Here we go!

21:20.500 --> 21:22.250
"Skylab Hurricane"!

21:24.380 --> 21:26.750
Hidari e iku ka?
Do I go left?

21:27.170 --> 21:29.300
Migi e yuku no ka?
Do I go right?

21:29.470 --> 21:32.010
Ue ni iku ka?
Do I go up?

21:32.220 --> 21:34.800
Shita ni iku no ka?
Do I go down?

21:35.640 --> 21:37.770
Achira kochira to
There are paths that go

21:38.270 --> 21:40.479
Michi wa aru kedo
Here and there, but

21:40.480 --> 21:43.270
Kitto heiki
I'm sure I'll be fine

21:43.440 --> 21:46.229
Tsukisusumu dake
Just keep moving forward

21:46.230 --> 21:51.649
Hitori ja fuan dakedo
This would be scary alone

21:51.650 --> 21:54.449
Issho dakara But you're with me

21:54.450 --> 21:57.080
Kowai mono wa nai yo
So there's nothing to be afraid of

21:57.370 --> 21:59.870
Donna michi demo
No matter the path

22:00.040 --> 22:02.540
Juuryoku mushi sa
We'll ignore gravity

22:02.870 --> 22:05.629
Chikara awasete Join forces

22:05.630 --> 22:08.420
Ima o tobikoeru
And fly beyond the now

22:08.590 --> 22:11.010
Donna toki demo
No matter the time

22:11.340 --> 22:13.800
Kimi ga iru kara
Because you're here

22:14.140 --> 22:16.600
Ai wa muteki sa
Love is invincible

22:16.930 --> 22:19.679
Skylab hurricane

22:19.680 --> 22:22.060
Todoke koe yo, sekai made
O voice, reach the world

22:22.310 --> 22:24.940
Kakenukete yo, uchuu e to
Charge on into space

22:25.190 --> 22:27.860
ROCKET ijou no SPEED de
At speeds greater than a rocket

22:28.150 --> 22:30.610
Juuryoku nante furikitte
Shake off gravity

22:30.820 --> 22:33.260
Toki o koete, mirai e to
And transcend time, toward the future

22:33.490 --> 22:36.030
Hikari ga sasu ashita made
To a tomorrow that shines brightly

22:36.280 --> 22:38.870
Mugen no hate no sono kanata e
Beyond the edges of infinity

22:39.120 --> 22:44.790
Kiseki o makiokoshite
Creating miracles

22:57.010 --> 22:58.470
Thank you!

22:58.800 --> 23:00.680
Okay, on to the next song.

23:00.930 --> 23:01.930
Next up is...

23:04.140 --> 23:05.190
Sonico!

23:09.060 --> 23:11.480
N-Nico, that...

23:13.190 --> 23:15.490
Is that the one that melts?!

23:26.380 --> 23:34.380
Next Episode Preview

23:27.040 --> 23:29.419
I've gone to Okinawa for a modeling shoot!

23:29.420 --> 23:30.589
Please calm down, Sonico.

23:30.590 --> 23:32.709
Mm, this food's delicious!

23:32.710 --> 23:33.710
You mustn't overeat!

23:34.090 --> 23:36.179
This swimsuit's kind of revealing...

23:36.180 --> 23:37.469
What's the meaning of this?!

23:37.470 --> 23:39.760
Next time, "Sonico Goes to Okinawa."

23:39.761 --> 23:41.390
Sonico Goes to Okinawa
